-# OC Change -- read-only copies imported from another Unfurl Cloud instance
-#
-# Without this an imported item just looks like one that mysteriously cannot
-# be edited: the policy prevents every write, and nothing on the page says why
-# or where the real item lives.
-#
-# Rendered on the merge request page, which is still server-side. The work
-# item page is a Vue app and gets the same banner from
-# oc/app/assets/javascripts/work_items/components/replica_banner.vue; keep
-# the two in step.
-#
-# A surrendered item needs its own words. It is read-only for a different
-# reason -- it is ours, being given away, and frozen so that nothing is edited
-# here while the other instance takes it over -- and it has no original to
-# link to yet, because the instance receiving it has not published its copy.
-# Shown the imported wording, it would read as a copy of an item that does not
-# exist anywhere.

- replica = issuable.oc_replica
- if replica&.read_only?
  .gl-alert.gl-alert-info.gl-p-4.gl-mb-5
    .gl-alert-body
      - if replica.state_surrendered?
        = _('Being transferred to another Unfurl Cloud instance, and read-only until it arrives there.')
      - else
        = _('Read-only copy of an item on another Unfurl Cloud instance.')
        - if replica.source_web_url.present?
          = succeed '.' do
            = link_to _('View the original'), replica.source_web_url,
              target: '_blank', rel: 'noopener noreferrer'
